## Section 1: Introduction

### 1.1 Purpose

This document specifies the requirements for MyCalTravels, a web platform serving a single travel writer/agent (Myah) and her clients.

### 1.2 Scope

MyCalTravels provides:
- **Public site** — Feed homepage, blog, guides, reviews, videos
- **Admin CMS** — Block-based content editor for posts/guides/reviews
- **Client portals** — Travel Information Wall per trip, accessible via magic link
- **Itinerary Builder** — Structured itinerary creation with beautiful client rendering
- **Admin Notepad** — Private per-portal logistics scratchpad
- **Theme System** — Semantic colour tokens driven by admin settings

### 1.3 Key Architectural Pivot (v5.0)

The project pivoted from a Canvas-style design tool to a **block-based content system** in v5.0. The Canvas system is frozen and pending deletion.

**Core principle:**
> Developer controls design. Template controls layout. Writer controls content. Settings control brand. System controls hierarchy.

**What was rejected:**
- CanvasElement for writers
- Moveable/drag/resize/rotate for writers
- Properties panels with per-element styling
- Free-form layout
- Full colour customisation
- General-purpose design tools

**What replaced it:**
- Semantic content blocks (Title, Body, Hero, Gallery, etc.)
- Templates define structure (which blocks allowed, order, required/optional)
- Portal Wall for client trip delivery
- Curated colour palettes (not free-form pickers)
- Named hero presets (no colour pickers)
- Admin Notepad for one-off logistics

