## Section 3: Block System (Content)

### 3.1 Overview

Posts, guides, and reviews are composed of ordered **content blocks**. Each block is one content type with one data model, one editor, and one renderer.

### 3.2 Block Types (10)

| Block | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| Title | Section heading (level 1/2/3) |
| Body | Rich text (TipTap JSON) |
| Callout | Tip / warning / info variant |
| Hero | Full-width image with caption |
| Image | Single image with caption |
| Gallery | Grid of images |
| QuickFacts | Label/value pairs |
| Quote | Text + author |
| ProsCons | Two-column comparison |
| Verdict | Text + star rating |

### 3.3 Block Registry

- `BLOCK_REGISTRY` maps `BlockType` → definition (label, icon, `getDefaultData()`)
- Renderers receive `{ data, style }` — TemplateStyle has all design
- Switch-based rendering (refactor to registry if 20+ blocks)

### 3.4 Template System

- Templates define which blocks allowed + order
- `TemplateSection` has `label` + `state` (required/optional/disabled)
- `TemplateCreator` is the admin UI
- 3 starter templates: Story, Travel Guide, Review
- Live templates: edit affects all posts using them
- `version: 1` in layoutData for future versioning

### 3.5 Post Storage

- Post = `templateId` + ordered list of block instances
- Block instance = `{ id, type, data }`
- Content only (no x/y/width/height/coordinates)

