## Section 6: Portal Wall

### 6.1 Overview

Client-facing "Travel Information Wall" — a visual bulletin board where trip information is visible at a glance.

### 6.2 Data Model

`portal_items` table (unified pipeline):
- `source_type`: `library` | `portal_specific` | `itinerary`
- `content_library_id` (for library references)
- `itinerary_id` (for itinerary references)
- Inline fields for `portal_specific`: `title`, `type`, `category`, `file_path`, `text_content`
- `position` (ordering)

### 6.3 Rendering

Wall item types:
- `pdf` → card with icon + download link
- `image` → full-width image
- `text` → styled card
- `itinerary` → tile that opens full itinerary view

### 6.4 Hero Banner

- Fields: `hero_title`, `hero_subtitle`, `hero_image`, `hero_preset`
- Image takes precedence over preset
- Presets: 8 named options

### 6.5 Admin Preview

- Route: `/admin/portals/[id]/preview`
- Uses admin session (no magic link required)
- Preview banner: "Preview mode — this is what your client sees."
- Handles deleted/archived/inactive portals with status banners

