## Section 7: Itinerary Builder

### 7.1 Overview

Structured itinerary creation with beautiful client rendering. Attached to portal wall via `portal_items.source_type='itinerary'`.

### 7.2 Data Model

```
itineraries (soft delete)
  └── itinerary_sections
        ├── itinerary_days
        │     └── itinerary_segments
        └── itinerary_stays
```

**Segment types:** `activity`, `travel`, `meal`, `free_day`

**Key rules:**
- Flights = Travel segments (no separate flights table)
- Stays belong to one section (no cross-section spans)
- Sequential stays only
- Time-derived ordering (no manual reorder)
- Empty days render intentional placeholder
- Print stylesheet export (no PDF pipeline)

### 7.3 Client Rendering

- Time-grouped display (Morning / Afternoon / Evening)
- Segment card colours by type
- Travel cards for flights
- Stay banner ("where you're sleeping tonight")
- Empty-day placeholder: "No activities scheduled"
- Print / Save PDF via browser-native print stylesheet

### 7.4 Admin Editor

- Extracted into 9 focused components (~17-line wrapper page)
- Inline forms replace all `prompt()` dialogs
- 4 form primitives: AutosaveTextField, AutosaveDateField, AutosaveTimeField, AutosaveSelectField
- Autosave-backed editing (draft durability)
- Section date constraints propagate to stays and days
- Travel segments reveal flight-specific fields

### 7.5 Scope (V1 vs V2)

**V1 (shipped):**
- Sections, days, segments, stays
- Travel segments with flight fields
- Empty-day placeholder
- Print stylesheet

**V2 (deferred):**
- Options segments (A/B alternatives)
- Cruise mode (port schedule tables)
- Overlapping stays
- Group splits
- Attendees on segments

